COMPANY EMPLOYEE HANDBOOK (2026 EDITION)

SECTION 1: LEAVE POLICY
1.1 Casual Leave (CL):
- All full-time employees are eligible for 12 days of Casual Leave per calendar year.
- A maximum of 3 days of CL can be taken at a stretch.
- Unused CL does not carry forward to the next year.

1.2 Sick Leave (SL):
- Employees are entitled to 10 days of Sick Leave annually.
- For Sick Leave exceeding 2 consecutive days, a medical certificate from a registered practitioner is mandatory.

1.3 Privilege Leave (PL):
- Employees earn 1.5 days of PL for every month worked (18 days per year).
- PL can be accumulated up to a maximum of 45 days.

SECTION 2: REIMBURSEMENT & EXPENSES
2.1 Travel Reimbursement:
- Local travel for client visits is reimbursable.
- Use of personal two-wheelers is reimbursed at ₹4 per km.
- Cab expenses are capped at ₹800 per day unless pre-approved by a manager.

2.2 Food Allowance:
- Employees working past 9:00 PM are eligible for a dinner allowance of up to ₹350.
- Original bills must be uploaded to the portal within 7 days of the expense.

SECTION 3: WORK HOURS
- Standard work hours are 9:30 AM to 6:30 PM, Monday through Friday.
- Employees are expected to complete 9 hours in the office, including a 1-hour lunch break.
